    <h2 id="how-to-export">How to export</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open BudgetBaby and go to <strong>Settings → Data &amp; Backup → Export Data</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>CSV</strong> or <strong>PDF</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select the date range to export.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Export</strong>. iOS presents a share sheet.</li>
      <li>Choose a destination. Files, Mail, AirDrop, or any other share target.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Free tier limit.</strong> Free users can export as CSV once per month. Premium users
      have unlimited CSV and PDF exports. The export screen shows how many exports remain for the
      current month.
    </div>

