    <h2 id="csv-files">CSV file reference</h2>
    <p>
      A CSV export produces these files (only files with content are generated). Each is a plain
      comma-separated table with a single header row and one row per record.
    </p>

    <h3><code>BudgetBaby_Transactions.csv</code></h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>Date</code></td><td>YYYY-MM-DD</td><td>The transaction date.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Category</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Category name at export time.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Priority</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Display name: Essentials / Variable / Fun / Unplanned.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Amount</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td>Positive number, no currency symbol.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Currency</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Currency code or symbol (e.g. $, USD).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Payment Method</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Cash / Debit / Credit / Savings.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Note</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Optional user note. May be empty.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3><code>BudgetBaby_Categories.csv</code></h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>Name</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Category name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Priority</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Essentials / Variable / Fun / Unplanned.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Icon</code></td><td>Text</td><td>SF Symbol icon name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Monthly Budget</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td>Planned amount per period (may be empty).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Currency</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Currency code or symbol.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Sort Order</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Display order for the category list.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3><code>BudgetBaby_Bills.csv</code></h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>Name</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Bill name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Amount</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td>Bill amount per occurrence.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Currency</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Currency code or symbol.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Due Day</code></td><td>Integer</td><td>Day of month the bill is due.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Payment Method</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Cash / Debit / Credit / Savings.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Category</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Linked category name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Status</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Active or Inactive.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3><code>BudgetBaby_Subscriptions.csv</code></h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Column</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>Name</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Subscription name.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Amount</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td>Subscription amount.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Currency</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Currency code or symbol.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Frequency</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Monthly, Yearly, etc.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Next Billing Date</code></td><td>YYYY-MM-DD</td><td>Next charge date.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Category</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Provider category.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Status</code></td><td>Text</td><td>Active or Inactive.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Monthly Equivalent</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td>Amount normalised to a monthly figure for comparison.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Using CSV in Excel.</strong> Open Excel, go to Data → From Text/CSV, select the file,
      and ensure the delimiter is set to comma. Excel detects UTF-8 automatically. If date columns
      appear as text, use Text to Columns to convert them to dates.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Transactions CSV" caption="Each row is one transaction with date, category, priority, amount, currency, method, note.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Files</span><span class="dm-bar-title">BudgetBaby_Transactions.csv</span><span class="dm-bar-action">⋯</span></div>
