          <div>2026-03-02,Groceries,Variable,42.18,$,Debit,Trader Joe's</div>
          <div>2026-03-02,Coffee &amp; Cafe,Fun,4.85,$,Cash,</div>
          <div>2026-03-03,Transport,Variable,140.00,$,Credit,</div>
          <div>2026-03-04,Subscriptions,Fun,15.49,$,Debit,Netflix</div>
          <div>2026-03-07,Dining Out,Fun,84.20,$,Credit,Anniversary</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">UTF-8 · ISO-8601 dates · numeric amounts · display labels</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="pdf-contents">PDF contents</h2>
    <p>The PDF report is generated on-device and includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Financial overview.</strong> Period budget, total spent, remaining.</li>
      <li><strong>Spending by priority.</strong> Totals for each color (Essentials, Variable, Fun, Unplanned).</li>
      <li><strong>Spending by category, grouped by priority.</strong> Each color band lists its categories with totals.</li>
      <li><strong>Monthly bills and subscriptions.</strong> Names, amounts, due dates, statuses.</li>
      <li><strong>Savings goals.</strong> Target, current balance, progress percentage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Use CSV if you need the raw data, the PDF is intended for sharing or printing.</p>

    <h2 id="deleting-data">Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      If you want to reset BudgetBaby or remove your data entirely, see the dedicated
      <a href="/budgetbaby/delete-data">Delete Your Data</a> page for complete instructions. That
      page covers local data reset, cloud backup deletion, account deletion, and subscription
      cancellation.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
